schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: DAO (Decentralized Autonomous Organization) — Core Parts
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A group that manages shared money and makes decisions together through
    code-enforced rules rather than a bank, lawyer, or board of directors —
    reducible to four parts: treasury, proposals, voting, and smart
    contracts.
  source_traditions:
    - traditional community savings circles / ROSCAs (the article's explicit analogy)
    - Ethereum smart-contract infrastructure (the "vending machine" mechanism behind automatic execution)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used as the plain-language entry point before naming specific DAO
    tooling (Snapshot, Safe, Aragon) and real regen-space DAO examples.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - a DAO's treasury as the digital-native version of a shared community bank account
    - Local Nodes (ReFi DAO) as a DAO-adjacent, place-based organizing pattern rather than a single monolithic DAO
  important_distinctions:
    - decentralized (no single boss decides) vs autonomous (rules run automatically as code) — the article treats these as separate properties, not synonyms
    - off-chain signaling (Snapshot, gasless but not self-executing) vs on-chain execution (Safe/Aragon, enforced by code)
  tensions:
    - a DAO "encodes trust so it can't be lost, manipulated, or forgotten" vs the article's own caveat that it won't fix a group that doesn't already trust each other
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Reducing every DAO to "four core parts" risks flattening real
    differences in how treasuries are actually secured (single multisig vs
    layered governance), how proposals are vetted before a vote, and how
    much of the "autonomous" execution is genuinely code-enforced versus
    still requiring a trusted human signer (as the article itself notes for
    Snapshot).
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-is-dao.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  source_lineage: what-is-dao.md
